                <pb facs="0805" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13238: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-26T11:00:00+08:00">October 26, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 26—9:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. My number 51, October 7, 4 p.m., paragraph 3. Missionary party arrived safely
                    Paotow Suiyuan Province yesterday according to a telegram received by mission
                    headquarters here today. Repeated to the Department, Peiping, Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
